Ever wondered how people recolor their Aseprite UI? They use something called **Themes**. Here's how to get them!
### Find and download Theme
1. Navigate to Edit ⇨ Preferences ⇨ Theme
2. Press **["Download Themes"](<https://github.com/aseprite/themes>)**
3. Pick a style you like and download it
### Install Theme
1. Navigate to Edit ⇨ Preferences ⇨ Extensions
2. Press "Add Extension"
3. Select the Theme file you just downloaded
4. Press "Ok"
5. Return to the Theme tab under Preferences
6. Click on your new theme and press "Select"

You'd like to have full control over your color customization? **[Check out this tool](<https://thkaspar.itch.io/theme-preferences>)**
